# Response headers for the deployed game (__KEY__.pages.dev). Cloudflare Pages
# reads this file from the root of the build output; Vite copies public/ into
# dist/ verbatim, so committing it here is what ships it. It is the same policy
# as Hypersweeper's (apps/hypersweeper/public/_headers, which explains each
# choice and the format's traps at length):
#
#   - one `/*` rule only — Cloudflare merges every matching rule and browsers
#     enforce every CSP they are sent, so a second rule could only narrow this
#     one, never widen it for a subpath;
#   - applied at the edge by Cloudflare, and to `vite dev` / `vite preview` by
#     the shared preset's `securityHeaders` plugin (packages/vite-preset), which
#     parses this very file — so the e2e smoke test runs under the real policy;
#   - the PR preview inserts `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` into the `/*` block at
#     deploy time (.github/workflows/pr-preview.yml), which is why the pattern
#     line must stay exactly `/*`.
#
# The Cloudflare Web Analytics origins are allowed, as in Hypersweeper's, so
# turning that on in the dashboard needs no policy change. No extension, so the
# service worker's precache glob does not pick it up.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
